  "history": {
    "claims": [
      {
        "text": "At Jade Dragon River in southern border, Fang Yuan waits for Ye Fan’s first fortuitous encounter and recalls Ye Fan’s later path from the Biography of Ye Fan.",
        "chapters": [
          680
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "intro",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "char_fang_yuan",
          "char_ye_fan"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "In that memory, after a riverside rank four Gu Master inheritance lets Ye Fan survive and grow in the wild, he grabs a huge opportunity and obtains black yellow mother qi Gu. The same recollection also places a daoist master inheritance in that rise, and says Ye Fan then wins nine out of ten times when rock gambling and dominates southern border gambling dens. Chapter 680 does not state the Gu’s rank, path, or direct effect.",
